# THE DETERMINISM RULE

# URL and keys come from http-client.env.json. Local values are the default; to test the deployed app, choose azure at the top right of this editor.

### 1. Replay demo. Watch the console for lines like:
#   IsReplaying=False | DateTime.UtcNow=10:00:00.120 vs CurrentUtcDateTime=10:00:00.050 | Guid.NewGuid=3f2a… vs context.NewGuid=9c1e…
#   IsReplaying=True  | DateTime.UtcNow=10:00:01.480 vs CurrentUtcDateTime=10:00:00.050 | Guid.NewGuid=b7d0… vs context.NewGuid=9c1e…
#   ... five lines, one per run. The left values change on every replay; the right values never do.
# The "Calling step N" lines (replay-safe logger) print once each.
POST {{baseUrl}}/determinism/replay-demo
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}

### 2. The broken orchestrator: send this a few times, then check the results.
# Expect nearly all of them to show runtimeStatus "Failed" with "Non-Deterministic workflow detected".
# (In the test run, 6 of 6 failed. A run occasionally survives by luck.)
# @name broken
POST {{baseUrl}}/determinism/broken
x-functions-key: {{functionKey}}

### Result of the last broken run
GET {{broken.response.body.$.StatusQueryGetUri}}
